      "message": "As of PS6, your CL still touches multiple lines where it\u0027s only applying formatting and not making any actual changes. Normally you\u0027d want to send a separate CL for review to fix a file\u0027s formatting, and you put the substantive CL based on top of it, thereby making the reviewer\u0027s work easier.\n\nIn this particular case, I don\u0027t really see why these changes should be done, because when I run `gofmt` on the file, it does not produce any of these changes. See [here](https://screenshot.googleplex.com/7gwXFjR68EJViRT) for a screenshot of the only changes produced by running `gofmt` on my own machine.\n\nAs a rule, when sending CLs for review, we try to make reviewers\u0027 lives easier by including the minimal set of changes. This is not just a personal courtesy; it is genuinely helpful for ensuring good outcomes for the code review process - the lesser the cognitive load, the better the feedback. (\"Better feedback\" in the sense of \"higher quality\", not in the sense of \"positive\".)",
